{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And He will grant you compassion and have compassion on you.</b> The intention of this statement here is that since He commanded concerning the wayward city that the entire city be killed by the sword, even their livestock — this deed will breed the trait of cruelty in a person's heart, as the Ishmaelites, the band of murderers, have told us concerning the king's decree: that they feel a great craving at the time they kill a man, and the root of compassion has been cut off from them and they have become cruel. So too this trait itself will take root in those who slaughter the inhabitants of the wayward city. Therefore He told them a promise, that HaShem will grant them compassion — even though nature breeds cruelty in them, the source of compassion will flow into them anew, instilling the force of compassion to nullify the force of cruelty born in them through the power of the deed." "And its saying <b>and have compassion on you</b> alludes to this: that all the while a person is in the category of a cruel nature, so too HaShem will deal with him accordingly — for HaShem, blessed be He, shows compassion only to one who is compassionate." "And its saying <b>and multiply you</b> intends to comfort the people when they see that a breach has opened through the loss of the people of an entire city at once; therefore He promised them that their heart shall not be dismayed, for He will multiply and fill the shortage with abundant increase. And its saying <b>when you hearken</b> gives a reason for His promise, for in truth if the burning of the people of the wayward city had been for human vengeance, there would be room to be drawn after the deed — but not so now, when the deed is solely for the reason of accepting the commandment of the King. And that is its saying <b>when you hearken to the voice of HaShem to keep all His commandments</b> — for when they execute judgment on the wayward city, it is as though they fulfilled all the commandments of HaShem, as they said, of blessed memory (Sanhedrin 111a)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:17:27.720270490Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}